import DubC2.Horseshoe

/-!
# Horseshoe obstructions on the zero-entropy frontier (generated)

Generated by `DubC2/xhorse.py --emit-frontier` from `DubC2/data/transform/xh/xh_frontier.jsonl`,
the horseshoes that `DubC2/xfrontier.py` reads off the exact follower automaton of a cell
(two closed walks at a branching state).  These are the cells left open by the length-bounded
search of `DubC2/HorseshoeAtlas.lean`; one theorem per witness, since a single word has up to
190 letters.  Statements about the certificate method, not about the orbits.

## References

* [Oda26] Y. Odagiri, *Finite graph certificates for composite terms in rational floor sequences*,
  Zenodo, doi:10.5281/zenodo.22997709 (2026).
-/

